<title>INDIA: India's Century Tex favours share split.</title>
<headline>India's Century Tex favours share split.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's Century Textiles and Industries Ltd said on Tuesday its board of directors had recommended a sub-division of the firm's equity shares.</p>
<p>The 100 rupee face-value shares will be split into shares with a face value of 10 rupees each.</p>
<p>&quot;The board has recommended sub-division of equity shares from 100 rupees to 10 rupees and a resolution for the above will be placed for shareholders at the ensuing annual general meeting, the firm said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
